#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0554-D expect=noViolation domain=APAE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when, in an Associated Persons dataset (DOMAIN starting with AP), APID is not present.
#note "AP-domain positive control, added by the R-5.25 wave-3 split: DOMAIN=APAE (prefix AP) and the APID column is present -> the associated-persons identifier requirement is satisfied ⚠ CLASS-UNREACHABLE IN PRODUCTION: this rule inherits CDISC-CG0554's Scope.Classes.Include [EVENTS, INTERVENTIONS, FINDINGS, FINDINGS ABOUT], and APAE resolves to NO class - DomainClassMap carries no AP entry and CustomDomainClassDetector.detectClass finds none of APAETERM/APAETRT/APAEQNAM/APAETESTCD - so ScopeMatcher.describeClassMismatch is strict-on-null and DatasetRuleResolver never emits the rule for an APAE dataset. The harness cannot say so: with no class= declaration describeScopeMismatch routes the class axis to describeAdamClassMismatch, which deliberately refuses SDTM class scopes, so this fixture passes the pre-gate that production would fail. Kept as the AP-branch expression coverage it is; the production-reachable scenario is the -AE sibling in this directory. Do not change the Scope - it is inherited by the whole CG0554 family."
dataset APAE label="Associated Persons AE"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col APID type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col APSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APAE | AP-001 | 1
---
